nd no train_done, bootstrap writes train.sh from the library asset (data/agent/_ASSETS/train.sh - nanochat speedrun pipeline: dataset, tok_train, base_train, chat_sft, torchrun on nvidia-smi GPU count) and nohups it with a pidfile guard; knobs via NANOCHAT_TRAIN_ARGS (default --depth=20; speedrun scale is --depth=24 --device-batch-size=16 --fp8). The service load-retries every 60s in mode waiting, so verdicts start on their own when base weights land; sft lands later - a service restart upgrades the loaded source. boot_error only fails the bootstrap report when training is not_needed - waiting-while-training is ok.\",\n    \"tags\": \"phase5b\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786843815148\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Bootstrap converges stale services (2026-08-16): /status reports pid and stale_script (file mtime newer than process start). When bootstrap finds a service answering but stale, it kills that pid and relaunches -> service: relaunched. Without this, a repo update left an old process holding the port reporting already_running while running last weeks code - bit the owner twice. One manual kill is needed only for services started before this shipped (they report neither field).\",\n    \"tags\": \"phase5b\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786844579176\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"First real training run (owner 5090, 2026-08-16): pipeline worked end to end (dataset, tokenizer trained into the base dir, model built) then OOMed on step one - base_train device-batch-size default 32 is an 80GB-card number; and without FlashAttention 3 the SDPA fallback cannot do sliding windows so SSSL runs terribly (nanochat warns both). NANOCHAT_TRAIN_ARGS default is now --depth=20 --device-batch-size=8 --window-pattern=L (consumer ~32GB); drop batch to 4 if still OOM - grad accum keeps the total batch identical, and chat_sft inherits device_batch_size from pretrain meta so one setting sizes both stages. train.sh exports PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True. Because train args are read from botd at bootstrap time, a failed run is retuned by editing botd.properties and rerunning bootstrap - no pull needed.\",\n    \"tags\": \"phase5b\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786844940379\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Phase 6 landed (2026-08-16): the resident service trains for real. trainer_real in the service asset: candidate deepcopy of the live model, AdamW at MODEL_TRAIN_LR, mixed mini-batches per MODEL_MIX (fresh curriculum from ingest via render_sample, replay reservoir capped 4096 in replay.jsonl, standard data from the base dirs parquet shards or standard.txt fallback), 1-in-10 fresh docs held out (heldout.jsonl, never trained). Gate every MODEL_GATE every= steps: cand must not regress on held-out standard beyond regress= AND must be <= live on held-out curriculum; pass -> ring checkpoint (cpt-<step>, keep 5) + promote via NanochatScorer.from_parts through the double buffer; fail streak of fails= -> candidate resets to live weights. All settings ride the bootstrap launch line so a service relaunch picks up botd changes. Verified on a fabricated tiny nanochat base (CPU): promote/hold/reset all exercised; serving uninterrupted through 40+ promotions. Owner calls (replay ratio MODEL_MIX, gate thresholds MODEL_GATE) shipped as proposed defaults pending veto.\",\n    \"tags\": \"phase6\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786892344268\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Process lesson (bit three times, 2026-08-16): killing processes by pattern match kills your own shell - the bash -c command text contains the pattern. And `cd X && nohup python ... &` backgrounds the whole list, so $! is the SUBSHELL pid, not pythons - pid files written that way lie, and kill $(cat pidfile) silently no-ops after the subshell exits. Reliable: scan /proc matching the executable path in cmdline[0] plus an argument, excluding os.getpid(); or write the pidfile from INSIDE the nohup-ed script ($$).\",\n    \"tags\": \"process\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786892344869\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"NANOCHAT_DIST (2026-08-16): multi-node base training through the same self-bootstrap. Setting nnodes=2,rank=<node>,master=IP:PORT,iface=<NCCL iface> rides the train.sh launch line as arg 4; empty = single-node --standalone unchanged. Rank 0 trains the tokenizer and writes train_done; other ranks download data (filelock-deduped on shared dirs), wait for tokenizer.pkl+token_bytes.pt, and join the torchrun rendezvous; iface exports NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME. The base dir must hold identical data on all nodes (NFS or pre-sync). Malformed specs (missing port) fail fast with a FATAL line. Built for the owners DGX Spark pair over ConnectX-7; ray is not involved - nanochat is plain torchrun DDP. Verified by dry-run harness (fake nvidia-smi/torchrun/python): correct torchrun args in single, rank-0, rank-1 modes; rank-1 tokenizer wait and train_done guard; bad-spec rejection.\",\n    \"tags\": \"phase6\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786894731163\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Phase 6b (2026-08-16): the gate measures the job, and the metrics are real. Gate: once >=4 held-out salience pairs exist, both candidate and live GENERATE verdicts on agree_n held-out pairs with THE serving prompt (salience_prompt/parse_salience shared between scorer and gate); agreement = 1 - mean|gen - frontier target|; promote needs cand_agree >= live_agree - agree_slack (MODEL_GATE gains agree_slack=0.05, agree_n=8) plus the standard-loss forgetting guard; under 4 pairs the loss proxy remains. Metrics: the service journals every served verdict, loss every 10 steps, and every gate row to runtime/agent/model/metrics.jsonl (self-capped at ~8k lines); agent-model-metrics returns downsampled loss series, gate history + pass count, and a 10-bucket verdict histogram; the mind tab renders them as sparkline/histogram/gatebar. Verified on the tiny base (agreement arithmetic exact: 0.5-default gen vs 0.75 targets = 0.75 both sides) and in headless Chromium.\",\n    \"tags\": \"phase6b\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786900393518\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"GPU release/resume (2026-08-17): the agents whole GPU footprint is the one service process. POST /shutdown (agent-model-service_stop; mind tab release GPU button) exits cleanly - ring/replay/heldout/metrics survive, only unpromoted candidate steps are lost. Resume via bootstrap: make_scorer now prefers the NEWEST RING CHECKPOINT (NanochatScorer.from_ring: build_model on the cpt dir, tokenizer from the base dir) over the birth checkpoint, so promoted CPT progress carries across restarts - this also fixed /promote in real mode, which wrongly constructed NanochatScorer(ring_dir) as if a ring dir were a base dir. Ring dirs are now time-named (cpt-<ts>-<steps>) so steps-counter resets cannot collide. SALIENCE=off (live key) keeps the service down across executive restarts.\",\n    \"tags\": \"gpu\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786963748247\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Phase 8a (2026-08-17): the pointer is split. The salience pointer stays the fast permissive lane; the USER-FACING pointer serves the service's /chat and advances only through the stricter USER_GATE (mode=manual|auto, soak_s + verdicts served AS the salience pointer, agree floor from the trainer's last gate, regress slack vs the last user promotion's held-out standard loss, check_s cadence). mode=manual parks the candidate as READY-with-evals for agent-model-user_promote (the mind tab button); a READY candidate is CLEARED the moment a newer promotion takes the fast lane - it qualifies only while it IS the canary. A watchdog re-audits the serving user pointer against the growing held-out pair set and auto-rolls-back to last_good on agreement decay; agent-model-user_rollback is the manual twin (one step, not a stack). User checkpoints are ring-pruning-protected; the pointer persists in user_pointer.json